// **The message improved by converting.** The arm said "'contains' requires a MutableArray of a
// comparable ('==') element type"; the declarations carry `T: Eq`, so the resolver names the bound
// and the type parameter that requires it. Same gain `to_mutable_set` got in F215.
//
// The same requirement `contains` already makes of an array: the element type has to support `==`,
// or "is this present" has no answer. A MutableMap's key and a MutableSet's element need no such
// check -- their declarations are already bounded `Eq + Hash` -- so the MutableArray is the only
// one of the four this can fail for.
fn main() {
    val ab = mutable_array_new<Channel<int>>()
    print(contains(ab, channel_new<int>()))
}
